# __NAME__ integration (Google) — what is left

`scripts/new-integration.py --google` wrote this crate, its migration and the
controller shim, in the shape every Google connection has: the SHARED Google
OAuth client, the shared account-key derivation, and `account_email` on the
row. This file lists what it did not do. Delete it when the list is done. The
full guide is `docs/adding-an-integration.md`; `talos-google-calendar-write`
is the finished example this was generated from.

A new Google scope set is a NEW connection (this crate), not a wider existing
one: every module granted `oauth/<provider>/…` holds whatever scopes that
connection carries.

## In this crate

- [ ] `cargo fmt -p talos-__ID__`: where a line wraps depends on the names
      just substituted into it.
- [ ] `src/lib.rs`: every `SCAFFOLD:` comment — the crate header (what the
      connection is for) and `REQUIRED_SCOPE`. `the_scope_was_filled_in`
      fails until the scope is real. Ask for the narrowest scope that does
      the job; the consent is refused if it comes back without exactly it.
- [ ] Read `migrations/__MIGRATION__` and keep or change it before it is
      applied anywhere. It already grants the table to `talos_admin_read`
      (it holds which account is connected, never a token); withhold it
      instead if that is wrong for this table
      (`talos-advanced-repository/tests/admin_read_role_grants.rs` fails
      until one or the other is done).

